<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xmlns:mstts="https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">
    <mstts:express-as style="friendly">
      <prosody rate="0.9" pitch="medium">
        <mstts:silence type="Leading" value="800ms"/>
        <emphasis level="moderate">Welcome</emphasis> to 
        <emphasis level="strong">"Rich Dad Poor Dad"</emphasis> by Robert Kiyosaki.
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        <prosody pitch="+10 percent">This transformative book</prosody> will challenge everything you thought you knew about <emphasis level="moderate">money</emphasis> and wealth building.
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        Through the contrasting lessons from his two father figures, Kiyosaki gently reveals the mindset that separates the financially successful, from those who struggle with money.
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        Are you ready to discover the principles that <emphasis level="moderate">can change your financial future forever</emphasis>?
        <mstts:express-as style="hopeful">
          <prosody pitch="+8 percent">
            Let's begin this journey together.
          </prosody>
        </mstts:express-as>
        <mstts:silence type="Tailing" value="1200ms"/>
      </prosody>
    </mstts:express-as>
  </voice>
</speak>